{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-16888","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-16145","text":"Dual- and Triple-Loop Machine Architecture"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-16890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16146","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE update (OS-010, 2026-04):"},{"id":"spn-16147","text":" With the introduction of OS-010 PULSE, the loop-interlock pattern documented here is now formalized as a manifest standard. Graphonomous, PRISM, AgenTroMatic, and every other portfolio loop declare their phases in "},{"id":"spn-16148","marks":["code"],"text":"<loop>.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-16149","text":" files (see "},{"id":"spn-16150","marks":["code"],"text":"/PULSE/manifests/"},{"id":"spn-16151","text":"), validated against "},{"id":"spn-16152","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-16153","text":". The \"dual loop\" is a special case of arbitrarily nestable PULSE loops — the same machine grouping works at any depth, and PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-16154","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-16155","text":" phase reads the inner system's PULSE manifest to discover the "},{"id":"spn-16156","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-16157","text":" boundary at runtime rather than hard-coding the integration. See \"Triple loop and beyond\" below."}]}],"id":"blk-16889","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-16891","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-16158","text":"The Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-16892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16159","text":"Graphonomous exposes 29 MCP tools. PRISM specifies 47. When both run in the same session (the benchmarking use case), the client sees 76 tools. Research shows:"}]},{"id":"blk-16893","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-16895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16160","text":"Tool selection accuracy degrades past ~30 tools (Opus 4: 49% correct at that scale)"}]}],"id":"blk-16894","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-16897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16161","text":"Each tool definition consumes 500–2,000 tokens of context before conversation starts"}]}],"id":"blk-16896","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-16899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16162","text":"76 tools can burn 40–80K tokens just on schema overhead"}]}],"id":"blk-16898","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-16900","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-16163","text":"The Insight: Machine Around the Loop, Not the Category"}]},{"id":"blk-16901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16164","text":"Instead of grouping tools by what they *touch* (graph write, graph read, belief, etc.), group them by "},{"id":"spn-16165","marks":["bold"],"text":"which phase of the closed loop the agent is in"},{"id":"spn-16166","text":" when it calls them."}]},{"id":"blk-16902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16167","text":"Both Graphonomous and PRISM are closed-loop systems. Their loops are structurally parallel and interlock when PRISM evaluates Graphonomous:"}]},{"id":"blk-16903","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Graphonomous (memory loop)          PRISM (evaluation loop)\n──────────────────────────          ───────────────────────\nretrieve  \"What do I know?\"         compose    \"What should I test?\"\nroute     \"What should I do?\"       interact   \"Run the test\"\nact       \"Do it\"                   observe    \"Judge the result\"\nlearn     \"Did it work?\"            reflect    \"What should change?\"\nconsolidate \"Clean up\"              diagnose   \"What's actionable?\""},{"id":"blk-16904","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-16168","text":"Graphonomous: 29 tools → 5 machines"}]},{"id":"blk-16905","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-16169","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-16170","text":" — \"What do I know?\""}]},{"id":"blk-16906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16171","text":"The agent calls this when it needs context before reasoning or acting."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-16908","spans":[{"id":"spn-16172","text":"Action"}]},{"id":"blk-16909","spans":[{"id":"spn-16173","text":"Replaces"}]},{"id":"blk-16910","spans":[{"id":"spn-16174","text":"Description"}]}],"id":"blk-16907","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-16911","spans":[{"id":"spn-16175","marks":["code"],"text":"context"}]},{"id":"blk-16912","spans":[{"id":"spn-16176","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"}]},{"id":"blk-16913","spans":[{"id":"spn-16177","text":"κ-aware ranked retrieval with topology annotations"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16914","spans":[{"id":"spn-16178","marks":["code"],"text":"episodic"}]},{"id":"blk-16915","spans":[{"id":"spn-16179","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_episodic"}]},{"id":"blk-16916","spans":[{"id":"spn-16180","text":"Time-range filtered episodic nodes"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16917","spans":[{"id":"spn-16181","marks":["code"],"text":"procedural"}]},{"id":"blk-16918","spans":[{"id":"spn-16182","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_procedural"}]},{"id":"blk-16919","spans":[{"id":"spn-16183","text":"Semantic search scoped to procedural nodes"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16920","spans":[{"id":"spn-16184","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage"}]},{"id":"blk-16921","spans":[{"id":"spn-16185","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage_query"}]},{"id":"blk-16922","spans":[{"id":"spn-16186","text":"Standalone epistemic coverage (act/learn/escalate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16923","spans":[{"id":"spn-16187","marks":["code"],"text":"trace_evidence"}]},{"id":"blk-16924","spans":[{"id":"spn-16188","marks":["code"],"text":"trace_evidence_path"}]},{"id":"blk-16925","spans":[{"id":"spn-16189","text":"Weighted Dijkstra evidence path between nodes"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16926","spans":[{"id":"spn-16190","marks":["code"],"text":"frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-16927","spans":[{"id":"spn-16191","marks":["code"],"text":"epistemic_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-16928","spans":[{"id":"spn-16192","text":"Wilson interval uncertainty analysis"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-16929","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-16193","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-16194","text":" — \"What should I do?\""}]},{"id":"blk-16930","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-16195","text":"The agent calls this to decide whether to act, learn, deliberate, or escalate."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-16932","spans":[{"id":"spn-16196","text":"Action"}]},{"id":"blk-16933","spans":[{"id":"spn-16197","text":"Replaces"}]},{"id":"blk-16934","spans":[{"id":"spn-16198","text":"Description"}]}],"id":"blk-16931","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-16935","spans":[{"id":"spn-16199","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"}]},{"id":"blk-16936","spans":[{"id":"spn-16200","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"}]},{"id":"blk-16937","spans":[{"id":"spn-16201","text":"SCC/κ analysis with routing recommendation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16938","spans":[{"id":"spn-16202","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"}]},{"id":"blk-16939","spans":[{"id":"spn-16203","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"}]},{"id":"blk-16940","spans":[{"id":"spn-16204","text":"κ-driven deliberation over cyclic regions"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16941","spans":[{"id":"spn-16205","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"}]},{"id":"blk-16942","spans":[{"id":"spn-16206","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"}]},{"id":"blk-16943","spans":[{"id":"spn-16207","text":"Priority survey across active goals"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16944","spans":[{"id":"spn-16208","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_cycle"}]},{"id":"blk-16945","spans":[{"id":"spn-16209","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"}]},{"id":"blk-16946","spans":[{"id":"spn-16210","text":"Full triage → dispatch attention cycle"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16947","spans":[{"id":"spn-16211","marks":["code"],"text":"review_goal"}]},{"id":"blk-16948","spans":[{"id":"spn-16212","marks":["code"],"text":"review_goal"}]},{"id":"blk-16949","spans":[{"id":"spn-16213","text":"Coverage-driven act/learn/escalate gate"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-16950","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-16214","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-16215","text":" — \"Do it\""}